WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.770
You run three Claude Code
sessions. Then five.

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:06.370
Then you lose track of which one is stuck.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:12.690
agentnet gives every session a name,
a boss, a task list and an inbox.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.850
Name them. Give them a
boss. Watch them work.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:20.850
Know who is stuck.

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:26.570
The live map shows each agent's state, its
progress and its task list, as it changes.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.290
Stop being the message bus.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:36.930
Agents message each other and report to their
boss, so you stop copying text between windows.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.450
Keep what the last agent decided.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.930
When a task is done, the
agent leaves a decision note.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:48.570
The next agent searches
it before it starts.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:55.610
It runs on your own machine, on
localhost, with no extra account.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:59.690
Each agent is a real Claude
Code session on your own plan.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:07.010
agentnet is free and open
source under the MIT licence.

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:09.930
Clone it from GitHub and
spawn your first agent.
